      "title": "Software libraries",
      "description": "The outside libraries this layer's code imports or keeps vendored, one `software-library` node each. A dependency in `package.json` is a `software-library/1.0.0` node: the version and sha512 `bun.lock` pins, the registry tarball, the SPDX licence read from the installed package, the range, whether it is a dev dependency, and the files that import it (`usedBy`). A bundle kept under `scripts/assets/vendor/<name>/<version>/` (LHC-Forms, the NLM Form Builder, jQuery, ucum-lhc) is a `software-library/1.1.0` node marked `vendored`: name, version, tarball and sha512 from its `vendored.json`, and its licence from its own licence file (an NLM notice the SPDX list does not carry is a `LicenseRef-`). The imports inside a bundle are not this layer's, so they name no node (owner, 2026-10-26: \"A. Record as vendored\"). GENERATED, never hand-edited: `bun run cat libraries:derive` writes it and `libraries:check` fails on a stale node, an import no node names, a shim no node names, and a vendored file whose bytes are not the ones its `vendored.json` records. The kind is cat-harness's (bean `jbvi`); this layer keeps its own nodes because it pins its own versions.",
      "readmePath": "libraries/README.md",
